@title Damaged project opens as a recovered copy
@area Fixtures
# A project file cut short (a full disk, a bad copy). It is never edited in place: the readable part
# is written to a recovered copy beside it, the copy opens, and a warning says what happened.
open qa/fixtures/damaged-cut-short.novo
wait 30
expect "damaged"
expect "recovered copy"
expect "was not changed"
expect "beside the original"
expect "Recover a damaged project"
# Not "saved" or "no issues" until a person has checked it: the checks only see what survived.
expect "Recovered copy: check every page"
expect "Saved (recovered copy)"
expect "In the copy:"
shot recovered-copy
check_layout
check_blank recovered-copy
# The pill opens the account of what the copy holds and what was left out.
click_text "Recovered copy: check every page"
wait 6
expect "In the copy:"
expect "I have checked every page"
shot recovered-copy-account
check_layout
click_text "I have checked every page"
wait 6
shot recovered-copy-checked
expect "No issues"
